The owner applies this to the fork and bumps the `rev` the root Cargo.toml pins for
hayro-jbig2, hayro-jpeg2000 and hayro-ccitt; `tools/state.sh main-checkout` lists it until then.

The extended reference template of a generic region (ITU-T T.88 sections 6.2.5.3 Figure 3(b),
6.2.5.4, 7.4.6.2 bit 4, 7.4.6.3 Figure 50). The pinned codec reads EXTTEMPLATE and ignores it: it
parses four AT pixels where the segment carries twelve, starts the arithmetic decoder sixteen bytes
early, and draws a wrong bitmap without a refusal. Annex K item 7 (codeStreamTest1_TT7.jb2)
exercises it. That stream departs from T.88 elsewhere too (ADR 1459 section 2), so it is refused
before its generic region is reached; with those departures set aside on a scratch copy, its page
differs from the reference in 1 746 pixels before this patch and in none after. Independent of
hayro-jbig2-symbol-dictionary-bounds.patch: each applies with or without the other.

